# Backend configuration this product owns. Ships empty and stays empty upstream, so nothing you
# add here can conflict with a boilerplate update.
#
# Every backend service, the migrator and the notification workers read this file. Compose merges
# it underneath each service's `environment`, which means:
#
#   - a key the boilerplate already sets cannot be shadowed from here. Those keys are all
#     `${NAME:-default}` interpolations, so the deployment's own `.env` is what overrides them.
#   - a key only this product knows about needs no edit to any file the boilerplate owns.
#
# Values are literal: Compose does not interpolate `${...}` inside an env file, and quotes are
# kept. Secrets do not belong here -- add them to the manifest in docker/secret-entrypoint.sh so
# every runtime receives them the same way.
#
# Kubernetes has the same seam under `config.extra` in .helm/values.yaml, and a native host reads
# the equivalent keys straight from its own .env.production.
#
# BILLING_LEDGER_URL=https://ledger.internal.example
